# SvelTeX

**SvelTeX** is a Svelte preprocessor. It lets you write **Markdown**, **LaTeX**
math and syntax-highlighted **code** directly inside Svelte and SvelteKit
projects — without giving up any of Svelte's interactivity.

Every page of this site is a single `.sveltex` file: Markdown on the outside,
Svelte on the inside. The site is built as static HTML by **SvelteKit**, and
the entire build runs on **Deno**.

## Explore the showcase

| Page                      | What it demonstrates                        |
| ------------------------- | ------------------------------------------- |
| [Markdown](/markdown)     | Headings, lists, tables, quotes, emphasis   |
| [Code](/code)             | Fenced and inline syntax highlighting       |
| [Math](/math)             | Inline and display math, typeset by MathJax |
| [Diagrams](/diagrams)     | LaTeX/TikZ pictures rendered to SVG         |
| [Components](/components) | Interactive Svelte components in Markdown   |
| [Blog](/blog)             | A post driven by YAML frontmatter           |

## One paragraph, three notations

Prose, `inline code`, and inline math like $E = mc^2$ all sit in the same
sentence. Display math gets its own centred block:

$$
e^{i\pi} + 1 = 0
$$

> **Accessible by default.** SvelTeX emits assistive MathML alongside the
> visual math, so screen readers can announce every expression.
